          "uid": "0sr2ea744i612kd9nuhvt905me@google.com",
          "title": "Quiz C17 🤠",
          "start": "2026-10-02",
          "endExclusive": "2026-10-03",
          "description": "Study Guide\n\n- Process of Fossilization\n\n- Major rock types: igneous, metamorphic, sedimentary\n\n- In which rock type do fossils tend to form?\n\n- Index Fossils & what they tell us\n\n- Law of Superposition = Relative Dating of Fossils\n\n- Absolute Dating - using Half-Life (you'd better be able to read half-life graph...)\n\n- Earth's Major Eras: Paleozoic, Mesozoic, Cenozoic\n\n- Paleozoic - the age of the Monster Amphibians\n\n- Mesozoic - the age of the Monster Reptiles & radiation of life forms (mammals...)\n\n- Cenozoic - what marks the beginning of the Cenozoic era (think asteroid...)\n\n- Early Earth - atmosphere, what the place was like, chemicals... Suitable for life?\n\n- Age of the Earth & How we know (hint: absolute dating)\n\n- The Urey-Miller Experiment = origin of organic compounds needed for life\n\n- Protenoid Microspheres - how are these related to early cells...?",
          "location": "",
          "assessmentScope": "Study Guide\n\n- Process of Fossilization\n\n- Major rock types: igneous, metamorphic, sedimentary\n\n- In which rock type do fossils tend to form?\n\n- Index Fossils & what they tell us\n\n- Law of Superposition = Relative Dating of Fossils\n\n- Absolute Dating - using Half-Life (you'd better be able to read half-life graph...)\n\n- Earth's Major Eras: Paleozoic, Mesozoic, Cenozoic\n\n- Paleozoic - the age of the Monster Amphibians\n\n- Mesozoic - the age of the Monster Reptiles & radiation of life forms (mammals...)\n\n- Cenozoic - what marks the beginning of the Cenozoic era (think asteroid...)\n\n- Early Earth - atmosphere, what the place was like, chemicals... Suitable for life?\n\n- Age of the Earth & How we know (hint: absolute dating)\n\n- The Urey-Miller Experiment = origin of organic compounds needed for life\n\n- Protenoid Microspheres - how are these related to early cells...?"
